        "problem": "Plot the graph of the parametrically defined curve\n\n$$\nx=t(t-6), \\,\\,\\, y=t^3, \\quad -2\\leq t \\leq 2.\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t(t-6).$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $16$ | $7$ | $0$ | $-5$ | $-8$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t^3.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $16$ | $7$ | $0$ | $-5$ | $-8$ |\n| $y$ | $-8$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $8$ |\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073429/assets/f15f25af0c4804dc811a0ab231ba2ef3ecce2ecd12501a1f2d8b9e34b71a505b.png)",
